        <h2>Leading radiation therapy in San Antonio</h2>
        <p>At Mays Cancer Center, home to UT Health San Antonio MD Anderson Cancer Center, we offer remarkable precision with the utmost compassion. We use special tools and techniques, such as deep inspiration breath hold (DIBH), to help protect your long-term health.</p>
        <p>We partner with MD Anderson Cancer Center to bring a higher level of cancer care to people living in San Antonio and surrounding South Texas counties. In many cases, our radiation oncologists consult with MD Anderson's team to get additional research-based treatment recommendations.</p>

        <h2>What is radiation oncology?</h2>
        <p>Radiation oncology is a medical specialty where doctors use powerful energy beams like X-rays and electrons, called radiation therapy, to treat cancer in different ways. In some cases, radioactive sources may be placed directly in the tumor during surgical procedures.</p>
        <p>Our cancer experts work to maximize radiation therapy's cancer-destroying effects while decreasing its impact on your life as much as possible. Members of our team also lead research efforts to further expand treatment options for eligible patients.</p>

        <h2>Why choose us for radiation therapy to treat cancer?</h2>
        <p>We use sophisticated machines and specialized techniques to treat many types of cancer in children and adults. You can access most of these services at Mays Cancer Center.</p>

